  "information_for_contributors": "This grammar is derived from textmate/toml.tmbundle\n(https://github.com/textmate/toml.tmbundle), file Syntaxes/TOML.tmLanguage,\npinned to commit e82b64c1e86396220786846201e9aa3f0a2d9ca2 (2020-07-14,\n\"Update syntax to TOML v1.0.0-rc.1\").\n\nPatch summary (this repo, VSCode-TW5-Syntax):\n1. TOML 1.1 escapes: \\e and \\xHH accepted alongside the TOML 1.0 escape set, in\n   both single-line and multi-line double-quoted strings and in quoted keys. The\n   invalid-escape rule at each of these sites is rewritten from a negated\n   character class to a negative lookahead over the full valid-escape\n   alternation, so it still flags an escape none of the valid forms cover.\n2. TOML 1.1 optional seconds: time and datetime values accept HH:MM alone, with\n   the :SS(.fraction) group made optional at both sites that read a time.\n3. Quoted, dotted table-header keys ([t.\"k.k\"] and [[t.\"k.k\"]]) no longer split\n   at a dot held inside the quotes: the header key-segment match is widened\n   from [^.\\s]+ to accept a double- or single-quoted segment ahead of the\n   bare-segment fallback.\n\nThe grammar is renamed to the private scope source.toml.tw5-syntax (see\nscopeName below) so it can never register as, or override, a user's own\nsource.toml grammar or .toml file association: this extension ships no\nlanguage entry or file-extension claim for it, only the scope.\n\nUpstream licence (toml.tmbundle README.mdown), reproduced in full in this\nrepository's ThirdPartyNotices.txt:\n\"Permission to copy, use, modify, sell and distribute this software is\ngranted. This software is provided \"as is\" without express or implied\nwarranty, and with no claim as to its suitability for any purpose.\"",
